# Update Docs After Implementation

After implementing a feature, fix, or significant change, update the docs so they stay accurate.

## When to Update

- Add or modify API endpoints, CLI commands, or config
- Change project structure, module layout, or data flow
- Add or remove environment variables, dependencies, or databases
- Change scraping, training, or diagnostic pipeline behavior

## Where to Update

- `docs/context/core/SPEC.md` — concise repo spec (paths, flows, stack); keep in sync when architecture or contracts change
- `docs/context/core/REPO_RULES_FOR_AI.md` — AI placement/safety rules when conventions or high-risk areas change
- `docs/context/README.md` — topic index when you add or rename files under `docs/context/`
- `docs/context/core/ARCHITECTURE.md` — system design, components, API surface
- `docs/context/data/DATABASE.md`, `docs/context/data/ISTA_DATABASE_GUIDE.md` — DB usage and schema
- `docs/context/scraping/SCRAPER_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/context/scraping/WEB_SCRAPING_PROMPT.md` — scraping behavior
- Other files under `docs/context/<topic>/` as needed for the change
- `README.md`, `AGENTS.md` — high-level setup and usage

## Checklist (Post-Implementation)

1. List what changed (APIs, CLI, config, flows).
2. Identify which docs are affected (use the topic folders above).
3. Add or edit sections so the docs match the new behavior.
4. Update `docs/context/README.md` if you added or renamed docs under `docs/context/`.
